### Mattermost Server Version

11.8.4

### Operating System

Ubuntu

### Steps to reproduce

1. Host an action endpoint that always return:

```json
  {
    "update": {
      "message": "",
      "props": {
        "attachments": [
          {
            "text": "Updated message"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
```

2. Create an incoming webhook
3. Send a payload that includes an action that calls the above endpoint:

```bash
curl \
  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{
    "username": "bot",
    "icon_emoji": "robot",
    "attachments": [
      {
        "text": "Original message",
        "actions": [
          {
            "id": "update",
            "name": "Update",
            "integration": {
              "url": "https://example.com/action",
              "context": {}
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }' \
  'https://mattermost.example.com/hooks/...'
```

4. Confirm the message does use the "robot" emoji icon
5. Click "Update"

See for example: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f6fb6482-6621-4196-aee4-881cb3315d35

### Expected behavior

The avatar shouldn’t change.

### Observed behavior

The avatar changes to the default incoming webhook one.

